  "body": "## Summary\n\nDepends on #343. Minimize retained webhook evidence at the shared inbox boundary for PayPal, PlaceToPay and PayPhone before payload bytes reach SQL/encryption.\n\n- Preserve original-body authentication, provider/merchant bindings and existing worker trust rules.\n- Retain only bounded, typed fields needed by current processing; discard unused nested customer/card/URL/description fields.\n- Preserve exact valid historical redelivery and immutable references/ciphertext without a migration or backfill.\n- Reject changed financial/metadata/trust evidence on duplicate identity. New same-ID deliveries differing only in discarded fields deduplicate safely under concurrency.\n- Redact decrypted payload `Show` output and stop echoing malformed PayPal JSON parser input in public errors.\n\n## Verified tests\n\nCode commit: `b524dc04a7633443420195ccdfad8121034dda38`; later commit adds documentation only.\n\n- `cd tdf-hq && stack test --fast --rerun-tests`: **2564 examples, 0 failures**, full backend, including existing Datafast/PayPal regressions. Started 2026-09-15T00:44:35Z; successful completion observed by 00:47:38Z.\n- `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh`: **36 examples, 0 failures** against a guarded disposable PostgreSQL 16 database. Includes nine new persistence/legacy/concurrency tests plus the existing 27 retry/recovery cases; no provider HTTP calls. An initial sandbox Docker denial (exit 126) was retried with approval; actual successful test duration 15.9008 seconds.\n- Catalog audit with the unchanged failure gate: **1122 candidates, zero unreviewed/stale decisions**, exit 0; report generated 2026-09-15T00:44:25.156Z.\n- `git diff --check` passed; disposable test containers removed by the harness.\n- Intermediate focused provider suite: 92 passed before the final eighth pure test; the final full-suite result above includes it. These are synthetic/local results, not provider sandbox evidence.\n\nExact commands, source hashes, timing bounds and outcomes are in `docs/payments/notification-minimization-2026-09-14.md`. Existing compiler warnings and quality gates are unchanged. No public contract/UI/mobile runtime change, screenshot, native-device test or staging payment test is claimed.\n\n## Architecture / compatibility / risks\n\nADR 0116 documents the exact field projection and primary sources. Original callback bytes remain the input to authentication. Minimized PayPal JSON is not an original signed transport envelope and must not be reused for remote signature verification. PlaceToPay retains the exact signed fields. PayPhone remains an untrusted query trigger.\n\nNo SQL migration, historical purge, order/payment reference rewrite or API response change. Existing workers can parse retained fields, but all writers must be upgraded together: old writers still retain full bodies. Rolling back storage code reopens that risk; do not erase evidence or create replacement charges as rollback.\n\nHistorical ciphertext may contain unnecessary/prohibited fields; actual contents remain uninspected. Security/PCI and Ecuadorian privacy/legal review must govern any remediation. PlaceToPay's original body-derived event IDs remain unchanged, so this does not solve cross-ID semantic replay/amplification. Unsupported PayPal events stay unsupported/ignored; this does not implement new refunds, subscriptions, disputes or payouts.\n\n## Access / activation\n\nNo production deployment or live transaction. Both staging URLs remain healthy, but the fresh 2026-09-15T00:47:40.611Z read-only inspection lacked Fly authentication; dedicated staging GitHub secret names are absent. Provider sandbox accounts/credentials/contracts remain unverified and activation gates unchanged. Parallel staging qualification and its approved catalog repair are in #344; this code does not depend on that tooling PR.\n\n## Review order\n\n#331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 this PR. Draft only; do not merge automatically.\n",
